{"type":"done","text":"I'd book a 12-show loop from Richmond. It starts close to home in Charlottesville, VA (#5) and Harrisonburg, VA (#14), heads out through Pittsburgh, Columbus, Bloomington, IN (#4) and Athens, OH (#11), then swings south through Boone, Asheville (#1), Knoxville and Athens, GA (#3). It finishes in Wilmington, NC and Carrboro, NC (#2), which is a 2.6-hour drive back home.\n\nThe whole loop is 1,936 miles and 35.2 hours of driving, and it needs no off days just for driving. The longest drive is 5.6 hours, from Athens, GA to Wilmington, so it stays under your 6-hour limit. Nine of the twelve stops are towns under 250,000 where fans of Big Thief, Waxahatchee and Adrianne Lenker rank in the top 20. None of the stops overlap with the usual big-city tour list. Boone, at #29, is the one stop outside the top 30, and it works as a short hop before Asheville.\n\nBurlington, VT, Northampton, MA, Ithaca, NY and Portland, ME were left out because the drive from Pittsburgh was too long for one day or they didn't fit in 12 days. Philadelphia (#8) didn't make the route either.","turns":4,"usage":{"input":29603,"output":1201}}
